{"content":"**Fixed.** `shouldRetry` now gates success responses out before the body check (`lib/src/js/sync_retry_policy.dart:180`):

```dart
bool shouldRetry(int attempt, int statusCode, [String? body]) {
  if (!canRetryAfter(attempt)) return false;
  if (statusCode == 0) return true;
  if (statusCode >= 200 && statusCode < 400) return false; // success: never retry
  return isRetryableStatus(statusCode, body);
}
```

Pinned as suggested in `deterministicRetryTests` (`test/js/sync_http_retry_test.dart`): `shouldRetry(1, 200, 'rate limit exceeded')` and `shouldRetry(1, 302, 'throttled')` are `isFalse`. Also pinned end-to-end: a new echo-server fixture answers 200 with a body mentioning rate limiting and the dispatch loop is asserted to issue the request exactly once (hit counter, `successGateTests`). Both tests verified RED before the fix. `statusCode == 0` remains an unconditional transport-failure retry.
